;; Reviewed 2026-10-09 by the user (written by Claude, from the design,
;; the MACRO manual, the RMS and System Services manuals, LLVM's code
;; generator and the guest runs). Why this is right:
;; - Phase 16 step 3 (section 14, item 10), under -trap-location: each
;;   trap calls POC_TRAP with six arguments, by CALLS #6: as before the
;;   code, L_MODULE_NAME, the line and the column, then L_FILE_NAME, the
;;   file as poc opened it, and L_WHERE_<n>, the procedure, a counted
;;   string (.BYTE of the length, then .ASCII) made when the procedure's
;;   first trap needs it: VaxTraps.NodeDesc.Sum, VaxTraps.Outer.Inner,
;;   VaxTraps.Outer and "VaxTraps, module body", as LLVM's -trap-location
;;   names them, so that rtl/vax/PocRtl.mar's POC_TRAP writes LLVM's
;;   message, file:line:column: message (in procedure), with $FAO.
;; - Under -range-checks CHR's code is ^X0001000E: 14, the status's, in
;;   the low word, and 1 in the high word for "CHR argument out of range",
;;   since SHORT's trap, #14 alone, is code 14 too.
;; - Traps, run on the guest with the real runtime for each case, prints
;;   LLVM's messages to SYS$ERROR and ends with %X10000000 + 8 * c + 2
;;   where LLVM exits with c (output.expected, plain.expected).
